CORE PHYSICAL CONSTRAINTS (CRITICAL — KEEP VERBATIM)
All beings have real mass, inertia, and momentum
Shallow water behaves as a viscous, resistive fluid
Every step displaces liquid → drag → rebound
Liquid piles, shears, ripples, and rebounds naturally
No hovering, no sliding, no floating
Nothing is ever fully static — environment always moves
Motion continues across cuts

THE ALIEN CREATURES (PREY / FALSE PREDATORS)
A dense group of alien amphibious creatures inhabiting a small, enclosed pond.
They have rounded, bulbous bodies with soft, rubbery skin in vivid pinks, magentas, and neon greens. Their surfaces are textured with raised nodules and faint bioluminescent bumps. Each creature has a large, rounded mouth with soft organic interiors (no sharp teeth emphasis) and multiple short, tentacle-like legs that press heavily into the water surface.
From the tops of their heads grow curved, spiraled horn-like appendages banded in bright colors (orange, yellow, pink). These horns are flexible and organic, varying slightly between individuals to suggest herd diversity.
Their faces are expressive and cute — blinking eyes, subtle head tilts, twitching tendrils — but their behavior is erratic and reactive. They move in bursts, stop suddenly, change direction impulsively, and respond emotionally to disturbances in the water.

They appear to be hunters at first glance, but are ultimately prey when confronted with disciplined opposition.

THE HUNTERS (TRUE PREDATORS)
A coordinated horde of humanoid hunters entering the pond.
They have compact, sturdy, stocky builds designed for stability and endurance in shallow water. Proportions emphasize function over speed: broad torsos, thick thighs, reinforced joints, and wide stances for bracing against resistance.
They wear uniform, full-body armor suits in a saturated yellow-green color. The armor is modular and layered, with segmented plates over shoulders, chest, thighs, and calves. Surfaces are matte to semi-matte, utilitarian, and subtly worn — practical, not decorative.
Each hunter wears a rounded, fully enclosed helmet with smooth, minimal facial detail, creating an anonymous, insect-like presence. A thin vertical antenna or spike protrudes from the top of each helmet, used for sensing, coordination, or communication.
On their backs are rectangular backpack-like rigs, tightly integrated into the armor. Straps, belts, and fastening points are clearly visible, reinforcing an expeditionary, militarized role. These packs appear functional, carrying tools or systems rather than weapons.
They wield long, slender spear-like weapons designed for reach and control, not brute force. Spears are held with both hands or braced against the body, used for thrusting and pinning large creatures from a distance.
Their posture is disciplined and coordinated: feet planted wide, torsos slightly forward, movements deliberate. They operate in tight formation, facing the same direction, implying hierarchy, training, and group tactics.
They show no emotion, no hesitation, no flourish.
They are calm, methodical, and inevitable.

